From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:24:44 -0400
Subject: fix: an upgrade keeps its profile, and ordinary clicks stop
 destroying data

Crashpad init asks PathService for the crash-dump directory, which creates
~/Library/Application Support/Stedding before profile migration. An empty
folder, or one that holds only Crashpad, blocked the move out of Chromium's
folder, so the first launch of this series would open a blank profile.
Migration now runs first, and a Crashpad-only folder still receives the old
profile. A marker records that the secrets were encrypted under the Chromium
keychain item.

The keychain no longer mints a new key when the old item cannot be read, and
a fresh profile does not adopt Chromium's key. An existing profile copies
that key once under Stedding's name. HTTPS-First balanced mode follows the
registered pref, which was on while the effective check ignored it. macOS
no longer reads Google Chrome's External Extensions directory. DuckDuckGo
is the search fallback even when the regional list omits it.

The collapsed rail is 44 DIP, above the 42 DIP narrow threshold, so a hovered
row centred the close button on the favicon. A rail row is narrow until
hover-expand. A plain click selects a drifted pin; reset is Option-click or
the essentials badge. The drag ends before that choice, so a reset cannot
leave the window uncloseable. Peek starts off. The Space sleep timer starts
at Never, and sleep skips audible, captured, picture-in-picture, fullscreen
video, beforeunload and form tabs, and the on-screen split pane. Clear keeps
folders and opens a new tab rather than closing the window. Switching the
strip drops the visibility controller and the folder drag target before the
view is freed, and rebuilds them with the new strip. Move to Space and
Route to Space ids, which are a range rather than one switch case, are
handled for the horizontal strip. A link dropped on a folder is placed
before or after it instead of hitting NOTREACHED. Session writes fetch
SessionService at each write.

Horizontal tab mode stays.

Why: the next release must not open an empty profile, mint a key over saved
passwords, or crash on the horizontal-tabs toggle and a folder drop.
Removable when: profile migration, the keychain item and these behaviours
are upstream or the features are withdrawn.
